  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/f25561a25abf75f301cbd29c6d6c0e2a0b61a389b757c06cd883819642f30545.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCEF$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{BF}?$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{FA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA}$\n- $\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CF}$",
  "worked_solution": "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FA}-\\overset{\\to }{BA} & =\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{FB} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CF} & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
